From 56f1f2a184ec9c0b1c7c8da06ea05aa99ce828ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cat-s22 <>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:04:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] tt9-s22: lighter ABC multitap on the CPU; version 64.0-s22.2 (1649)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Suggestion bar: when cycling letters only the colours of the previous and the
  new letter are repainted (payload in notifyItemChanged), without the temporary
  ViewHolder of the "change" animation (0 ms, invisible) and without rebuilding the text.
- Click listeners created once per ViewHolder, not on every bind.
- Recycled view pool raised to 32: with more than 5 letters on screen, every new
  key (notifyDataSetChanged) inflated again the views that did not fit in the pool.
- No RelativeSizeSpan when the scale is 100 % (suggestions and status bar): same
  look, without forcing the slow measurement of spanned text.
- Status bar: not rewritten if the shown text does not change.
- Status icon: not resent to system_server/SystemUI if it does not change
  (cache reset on every input field start).
- ABC: accepting the previous letter no longer empties the list right before
  showing the letters of the new key (one empty render and two status bar changes less).
- Text before and after the cursor requested at the same time (two parallel
  requests) instead of one after the other: one editor round trip less per new letter.
